---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Camille Roux — Evolutionary Biology</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Camille Roux, CNRS researcher at ISEM, working on speciation, reproductive barriers, population genomics, and demographic inference."
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="page-motif" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <main class="page-content min-h-screen px-6 py-7 md:px-12 lg:px-20">
      <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl flex-col">
        <!-- Header -->
        <header
          class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-b border-[var(--line)] pb-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between"
        >
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[var(--green)]">
              CNRS · ISEM · Montpellier
            </p>
            <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-5xl">
              Camille Roux
            </h1>
          </div>

          <nav
            class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm text-[var(--muted)] md:justify-end"
          >
            <a href="#research" class="transition-colors hover:text-[var(--foreground)]"
              >Research</a
            >
            <a href="#work" class="transition-colors hover:text-[var(--foreground)]"
              >Selected work</a
            >
            <a href="#contact" class="transition-colors hover:text-[var(--foreground)]"
              >Contact</a
            >
          </nav>
        </header>

        <!-- Hero -->
        <section
          class="grid gap-7 border-b border-[var(--line)] py-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr] lg:items-end lg:py-14"
        >
          <div>
            <p
              class="max-w-3xl text-3xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-4xl lg:text-[2.65rem]"
            >
              I study how reproductive barriers emerge, accumulate, and shape the formation
              of species.
            </p>

            <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-[var(--muted)] md:text-lg">
              My work combines population genomics, demographic inference, comparative
              multi-species analyses, and method development.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div
            class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--card)]/90 p-5 shadow-sm backdrop-blur-sm md:p-6 lg:translate-y-1"
          >
            <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[var(--ochre)]">
              Current direction
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xl leading-snug md:text-[1.35rem]">
              Why do some lineages accumulate reproductive barriers faster than others?
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Research -->
        <section id="research" class="scroll-mt-8 border-b border-[var(--line)] py-12 lg:py-16">
          <div class="lg:pr-12">
            <h2 class="section-title">Research</h2>
            <p class="section-intro mt-4">
              I study the emergence of reproductive isolation between evolutionary lineages.
              Most of my work starts from population genomic data, but the broader aim is
              comparative: to understand why some groups accumulate barriers to gene flow
              faster than others.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3 lg:mt-10 lg:gap-5">
            <article
              class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--card)]/80 p-5 md:col-span-1"
            >
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--green)]">
                Speciation genomics
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                I use genomic data to estimate how genetic connectivity decreases along the
                continuum from populations to species, and to identify the demographic
                histories that shape this transition.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article
              class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--card)]/80 p-5 md:col-span-1"
            >
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--green)]">
                Methods and inference
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                I develop and use statistical tools for demographic inference, especially
                approximate Bayesian computation frameworks designed to compare alternative
                models of divergence and gene flow.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article
              class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--card)]/80 p-5 md:col-span-1"
            >
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--green)]">
                Comparative synthesis
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                I am interested in large-scale comparisons across species pairs, clades, and
                biological systems, with the aim of connecting population-scale processes to
                broader evolutionary patterns.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Current questions -->
        <section class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-12 lg:py-16">
          <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:gap-10">
            <div>
              <h2 class="section-title">Current questions</h2>
              <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-base leading-7 text-[var(--muted)] md:text-[1.0625rem]">
                A central question in my current work is why plants appear to establish
                reproductive barriers faster than animals. This result emerged from a large
                comparative analysis of genomic data across hundreds of species pairs and now
                opens a broader research program: identifying the biological mechanisms that
                accelerate or slow down the accumulation of barriers to gene flow.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
              <blockquote
                class="border-l-2 border-[var(--ochre)] pl-5 text-lg font-medium leading-snug tracking-tight md:text-xl"
              >
                Can population-scale dynamics of reproductive isolation help explain
                macroevolutionary differences in diversification?
              </blockquote>

              <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3.5" role="list">
                <li class="question-line">
                  How does gene flow decline with molecular divergence?
                </li>
                <li class="question-line">
                  Which genomic compartments contribute to reproductive isolation?
                </li>
                <li class="question-line">
                  Are plant-specific features, including cytoplasmic genomes, involved in
                  faster barrier accumulation?
                </li>
                <li class="question-line">
                  Can comparative population genomics provide quantitative links between
                  microevolution and macroevolution?
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Selected work -->
        <section id="work" class="scroll-mt-8 border-b border-[var(--line)] py-12 lg:py-16">
          <h2 class="section-title">Selected work</h2>

          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col divide-y divide-[var(--line)]">
            <article class="py-6 first:pt-0 lg:py-7">
              <h3 class="text-[0.95rem] font-semibold leading-snug md:text-base">
                François Monnet, Zoé Postel, Pascal Touzet, Christelle Fraïsse, Yves Van de
                Peer, Xavier Vekemans &amp; Camille Roux. 2025.
                <a
                  href="https://www.science.org/doi/abs/10.1126/science.adl2356"
                  class="text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                  >Rapid establishment of species barriers in plants compared with that in
                  animals.</a
                >
                <span class="font-normal text-[var(--muted)]">Science.</span>
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                A comparative population genomic analysis showing that, for a given level of
                molecular divergence, plant species pairs are less genetically connected than
                animal species pairs.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="py-6 lg:py-7">
              <h3 class="text-[0.95rem] font-semibold leading-snug md:text-base">
                Yannick Juvé et al. 2025.
                <a
                  href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09425-w"
                  class="text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                  >One mother for two species via obligate cross-species cloning in ants.</a
                >
                <span class="font-normal text-[var(--muted)]">Nature.</span>
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                A collaborative study on an unusual reproductive system in ants, connecting
                hybridization, clonality, and species boundaries.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="py-6 lg:py-7">
              <h3 class="text-[0.95rem] font-semibold leading-snug md:text-base">
                Christelle Fraïsse et al. 2021.
                <span class="text-[var(--foreground)]"
                  >DILS: Demographic inferences with linked selection by using ABC.</span
                >
                <span class="font-normal text-[var(--muted)]">Molecular Ecology Resources.</span>
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                A method and software framework to compare demographic models, estimate gene
                flow, and account for linked selection in population genomic data.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="py-6 lg:py-7">
              <h3 class="text-[0.95rem] font-semibold leading-snug md:text-base">
                Camille Roux et al. 2016.
                <span class="text-[var(--foreground)]"
                  >Shedding Light on the Grey Zone of Speciation along a Continuum of Genomic
                  Divergence.</span
                >
                <span class="font-normal text-[var(--muted)]">PLOS Biology.</span>
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                A conceptual and empirical contribution to thinking about speciation as a
                continuum rather than a binary transition.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="pb-0 pt-6 lg:py-7">
              <h3 class="text-[0.95rem] font-semibold leading-snug md:text-base">
                Camille Roux, Alice Ha, Arthur Weyna, Morgan Lodé &amp; Jonathan Romiguier.
                2024.
                <span class="text-[var(--foreground)]"
                  >The impact of social complexity on the efficacy of natural selection in
                  termites.</span
                >
                <span class="font-normal text-[var(--muted)]">Peer Community Journal.</span>
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                A comparative molecular evolution study asking how social organization affects
                the efficacy of natural selection.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Tools and approaches -->
        <section class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-12 lg:py-16">
          <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] lg:items-start lg:gap-12">
            <div>
              <h2 class="section-title">Tools and approaches</h2>
              <p class="mt-4 max-w-md text-base leading-7 text-[var(--muted)]">
                I like tools that make biological questions testable. Method development is
                not separate from empirical work in my research; it is often the way to turn
                vague evolutionary questions into measurable quantities.
              </p>
            </div>

            <ul
              class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2.5 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-3"
              role="list"
            >
              {
                [
                  "DILS",
                  "ABC inference",
                  "Population genomics",
                  "Comparative datasets",
                  "Simulations",
                  "Phylogenetic thinking",
                  "Meta-analysis",
                  "Reproductive isolation",
                ].map((tool) => (
                  <li
                    class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--card)]/70 px-3 py-2 text-center text-sm tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]"
                  >
                    {tool}
                  </li>
                ))
              }
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ERC direction -->
        <section class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-12 lg:py-16">
          <div class="max-w-3xl lg:ml-auto lg:max-w-2xl lg:pr-4">
            <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[var(--ochre)]">
              ERC direction
            </p>
            <h2 class="section-title mt-3">
              Toward a comparative theory of reproductive barrier accumulation
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-[var(--muted)]">
              The ERC project I am preparing will build on comparative population genomics,
              statistical modelling, and experimental perspectives to understand why
              reproductive barriers accumulate faster in some lineages than in others. The aim
              is not only to document patterns of gene flow, but to identify the biological
              features that make the origin of species more or less likely.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Scientific life -->
        <section class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-12 lg:py-16">
          <div class="max-w-2xl">
            <h2 class="section-title">Scientific life</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-[var(--muted)]">
              I value collaborative scientific spaces: journal clubs, student discussions,
              method-oriented workshops, and conferences designed for exchange rather than
              display. My work has grown through collaborations across population genomics,
              molecular evolution, phylogenetics, and comparative biology.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Contact -->
        <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-8 py-12 lg:py-16">
          <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-12">
            <div>
              <h2 class="section-title">Contact</h2>
              <address class="mt-5 not-italic text-base leading-7">
                <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">Camille Roux</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-[var(--muted)]">CNRS researcher</p>
                <p class="text-[var(--muted)]">
                  Institut des Sciences de l'Évolution de Montpellier
                </p>
                <p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Montpellier, France</p>
              </address>
            </div>

            <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-[0.95rem] lg:pt-6" role="list">
              <li>
                <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--muted)]"
                  >Google Scholar</span
                >
                <a
                  href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=QppHnSsAAAAJ&hl=fr&oi=ao"
                  class="mt-1 block text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                  >scholar.google.com</a
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--muted)]"
                  >ISEM profile</span
                >
                <a
                  href="https://isem-evolution.fr/membre/roux/"
                  class="mt-1 block text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                  >isem-evolution.fr</a
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--muted)]"
                  >Science article</span
                >
                <a
                  href="https://www.science.org/doi/abs/10.1126/science.adl2356"
                  class="mt-1 block text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                  >science.org — plants vs animals</a
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--muted)]"
                  >Nature article</span
                >
                <a
                  href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09425-w"
                  class="mt-1 block text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                  >nature.com — cross-species cloning in ants</a
                >
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
